---
name: keep-pc-online
description: >-
  Use this to install, test, or remove the Windows fix that stops the Grok Bot
  desktop app from dropping a PC offline after it's been idle.
---
# Keep the Grok Bot PC online (Windows, no admin)

Problem: the Grok Bot desktop app marks a Windows PC "away" once its window has been out of focus for about 10 minutes, then drops the connection, so bots see the PC as offline.

Fix: a hidden per-user scheduled task named `GrokBot Keep Present` runs at logon and every 4 minutes. If the user has been idle for 5 or more minutes and the Grok Bot window isn't in front, the task brings it to the front. Everything lives in `%USERPROFILE%\GrokBotKeepPresent`, and each run adds a line to `keep-present.log` there. Side effect: after 5 or more minutes away, the user's first click may land on Grok Bot.

Run every command on the owner's chosen computer (Shell with its machineId). Get approval first.

## 1. Write the script
```powershell
$dir = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE 'GrokBotKeepPresent'
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force $dir | Out-Null
$script = @'
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$log = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'keep-present.log'
function Log($idle, $action) { "{0:yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss}`tidleSec={1}`taction={2}" -f (Get-Date), $idle, $action | Add-Content -Path $log }
try {
  Add-Type -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue @"
using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices;
public static class KP {
  [StructLayout(LayoutKind.Sequential)] public struct LII { public uint cbSize; public uint dwTime; }
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern bool GetLastInputInfo(ref LII p);
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern IntPtr GetForegroundWindow();
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern bool SetForegroundWindow(IntPtr h);
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern bool ShowWindow(IntPtr h, int c);
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern bool IsIconic(IntPtr h);
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern void keybd_event(byte k, byte s, uint f, UIntPtr e);
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern uint GetWindowThreadProcessId(IntPtr h, out uint pid);
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern bool AttachThreadInput(uint a, uint b, bool f);
  [DllImport("kernel32.dll")] public static extern uint GetCurrentThreadId();
  public static uint IdleMs() { var l = new LII(); l.cbSize = (uint)Marshal.SizeOf(l); GetLastInputInfo(ref l); return (uint)Environment.TickCount - l.dwTime; }
}
"@
  $idle = [int]([KP]::IdleMs() / 1000)
  $procs = @(Get-Process -Name 'Grok Bot' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)
  if ($procs.Count -eq 0) { Log $idle 'skip:not-running'; exit 0 }
  $fg = [KP]::GetForegroundWindow(); $fgPid = 0; [void][KP]::GetWindowThreadProcessId($fg, [ref]$fgPid)
  if ($procs.Id -contains [int]$fgPid) { Log $idle 'skip:already-foreground'; exit 0 }
  if ($idle -lt 300) { Log $idle 'skip:user-active'; exit 0 }
  $w = $procs | Where-Object { $_.MainWindowHandle -ne [IntPtr]::Zero } | Select-Object -First 1
  if (-not $w) { Log $idle 'skip:no-main-window'; exit 0 }
  $h = $w.MainWindowHandle
  if ([KP]::IsIconic($h)) { [void][KP]::ShowWindow($h, 9) }
  $me = [KP]::GetCurrentThreadId(); $dummy = 0; $fgThread = [KP]::GetWindowThreadProcessId($fg, [ref]$dummy)
  [KP]::keybd_event(0x12, 0, 0, [UIntPtr]::Zero); [KP]::keybd_event(0x12, 0, 2, [UIntPtr]::Zero)
  $att = $false; if ($fgThread -ne 0 -and $fgThread -ne $me) { $att = [KP]::AttachThreadInput($me, $fgThread, $true) }
  $ok = [KP]::SetForegroundWindow($h)
  if ($att) { [void][KP]::AttachThreadInput($me, $fgThread, $false) }
  Log $idle ("focused:ok=$ok")
} catch { Log -1 ("error:" + $_.Exception.Message) }
'@
Set-Content -Path "$dir\keep-present.ps1" -Value $script -Encoding UTF8
```

## 2. Install the hidden launcher and task
```powershell
$dir = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE 'GrokBotKeepPresent'
$vbs = "CreateObject(""Wscript.Shell"").Run ""powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -WindowStyle Hidden -File """"$dir\keep-present.ps1"""""", 0, False"
Set-Content -Path "$dir\keep-present.vbs" -Value $vbs -Encoding ASCII
$a = New-ScheduledTaskAction -Execute 'wscript.exe' -Argument "`"$dir\keep-present.vbs`""
$t1 = New-ScheduledTaskTrigger -AtLogOn -User $env:USERNAME
$t2 = New-ScheduledTaskTrigger -Once -At (Get-Date).AddMinutes(1) -RepetitionInterval (New-TimeSpan -Minutes 4)
$s = New-ScheduledTaskSettingsSet -MultipleInstances IgnoreNew -ExecutionTimeLimit (New-TimeSpan -Minutes 2) -AllowStartIfOnBatteries -DontStopIfGoingOnBatteries
Register-ScheduledTask -TaskName 'GrokBot Keep Present' -Action $a -Trigger $t1,$t2 -Settings $s -Description 'Brings Grok Bot to front after 5 min idle so the PC stays online'
```

## 3. Test
```powershell
Start-ScheduledTask 'GrokBot Keep Present'
Start-Sleep 5
(Get-ScheduledTaskInfo 'GrokBot Keep Present').LastTaskResult   # expect 0
Get-Content "$env:USERPROFILE\GrokBotKeepPresent\keep-present.log" -Tail 3
```
If the result is 0 and the log has a fresh line (usually `skip:user-active` or `skip:already-foreground` while someone is using the PC), it's working.

## 4. Remove
```powershell
Unregister-ScheduledTask -TaskName 'GrokBot Keep Present' -Confirm:$false
Remove-Item "$env:USERPROFILE\GrokBotKeepPresent" -Recurse -Force   # optional
```
